1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:03,875
Operators report consistent successful cluster deployments

2
00:00:03,883 --> 00:00:07,629
with pipeline post-configuration and successful cluster recoveries

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,426
using ZTF Orchestrator.

4
00:00:09,798 --> 00:00:14,057
Open Recover Infrastructure from Start Here, or Recover Cluster in Disaster

5
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:17,875
Recovery. Choose the intended datacenter and profile.

6
00:00:17,947 --> 00:00:21,711
If an open recovery exists, select Resume Recovery.

7
00:00:21,822 --> 00:00:25,961
This opens its saved snapshot and completed work instead of preparing another

8
00:00:25,961 --> 00:00:30,603
deployment. For a new recovery, review prerequisites, the Foundation

9
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:35,220
YAML, exact physical nodes and the linked post-configuration pipeline.

10
00:00:35,364 --> 00:00:38,023
Profile edits create a new draft revision;

11
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:40,775
they do not rewrite existing run snapshots.

12
00:00:40,911 --> 00:00:43,378
Review that revision before preparing the run.

13
00:00:43,556 --> 00:00:45,127
Archive preserves history;

14
00:00:45,306 --> 00:00:48,718
deletion is limited to unused, unlinked profiles.

15
00:00:49,124 --> 00:00:53,596
The recovery view leads with its current stage, any failure and the next required

16
00:00:53,604 --> 00:00:57,692
action. Expand stages or pipeline steps when you need detail.

17
00:00:58,041 --> 00:01:02,521
Deployment still needs the existing approval and exact destructive confirmation.

18
00:01:02,794 --> 00:01:05,872
This film shows a simulation, not a live rebuild.

19
00:01:06,122 --> 00:01:10,594
After Foundation completes, restore initial administrative access through the
approved

20
00:01:10,602 --> 00:01:14,700
bootstrap. Verify replacement authentication before later work.

21
00:01:14,889 --> 00:01:19,531
Then collect or record the required fresh PE identity, membership

22
00:01:19,582 --> 00:01:23,913
and health evidence. A failed certificate check is a collection problem;

23
00:01:24,049 --> 00:01:28,102
use the documented trusted or independent evidence path rather than

24
00:01:28,102 --> 00:01:29,765
bypassing the recovery gate.

25
00:01:30,085 --> 00:01:34,556
For failure or uncertainty, inspect the existing job and actual Foundation

26
00:01:34,692 --> 00:01:38,674
or Prism state. Record reconciliation before continuation.

27
00:01:38,916 --> 00:01:41,605
Completed configuration remains completed.

28
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:46,350
An eligible step zero eight registration retry requires confirmed absent registration

29
00:01:46,529 --> 00:01:51,171
and fresh health. Final infrastructure acceptance precedes workload restoration

30
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:52,836
through the backup platform.
